+config RISCV_CAPSTONE_TRAP
+	bool "Enter and leave protected programs through ordinary traps"
+	depends on RISCV_CAPSTONE_TASK && 64BIT && !SMP
+	default n
+	help
+	  The trap entry and exit of plan v5 step 3: every entry from U saves
+	  the user registers with their tags into 16-byte slots of the task,
+	  every return to a protected program loads them back, t6 keeps its
+	  tag across a trap from S, and a guard on every return to U checks
+	  that srevroot names the task's table. Needs a Sublet processor with
+	  supervisor references (QEMU x-capstone-supervisor-refs) and a
+	  firmware that keeps register tags across M traps.
+
+config RISCV_CAPSTONE_TRAP_SENTINEL
+	bool "Stop the kernel on a stray tagged kernel register"
+	depends on RISCV_CAPSTONE_TRAP
+	default n
+	help
